WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.833
A dashboard is useful only when its data and services are dependable.

00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:13.395
Health monitoring should cover collectors, queues, databases, storage, frontend services, clocks, notification channels, and upstream sources.

00:00:13.395 --> 00:00:20.524
Show stale data and failed ingestion clearly rather than presenting an apparently normal empty view.

00:00:20.524 --> 00:00:23.765
Track disk capacity before storage fills.

00:00:23.765 --> 00:00:31.758
Video and verbose logs can grow rapidly, and a full disk may stop ingestion or damage databases.

00:00:31.758 --> 00:00:37.591
Use capacity thresholds, retention enforcement, and protected free space for critical services.

00:00:37.591 --> 00:00:42.128
Monitor queue depth and processing delay to detect overload.

00:00:42.128 --> 00:00:50.554
Back up configuration, event data that must be retained, encryption material where appropriate, and documentation needed for recovery.

00:00:50.554 --> 00:00:55.523
A backup is not complete until restoration has been tested.

00:00:55.523 --> 00:01:00.492
Define recovery order, dependencies, responsible owners, and expected recovery time.

00:01:00.492 --> 00:01:04.597
Alert delivery can fail even when detection succeeds.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:12.158
Monitor email, messaging, mobile, or local notification paths and provide a visible queue for undelivered alerts.

00:01:12.158 --> 00:01:19.720
Important workflows need fallback contacts or local procedures instead of assuming one channel will always work.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.096
Plan for offline operation.

00:01:22.096 --> 00:01:30.090
Local collection and review may continue during an internet outage, while external enrichment and remote notifications pause.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:38.083
Document which functions degrade, how queued work is handled, and how the system reconciles after connectivity returns.

00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:46.077
Maintenance includes patching, certificate renewal, account review, database care, model or rule updates, and periodic recovery exercises.

00:01:46.077 --> 00:01:52.342
Schedule changes, preserve rollback options, and verify that data still flows after updates.

00:01:52.342 --> 00:01:59.472
Reliability is built through routine observation and practiced procedures, not assumed from a successful installation.
